{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1398303-honing-the-form-multiple-times","id":1398303,"title":"Honing the form multiple times?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-23T00:47:19-07:00","id":1398303,"title":"Honing the form multiple times?","content":"Hi there fellow wizards. I'm about to play a thyrsus mage in a forest full of bad spirits and most likely angry werewolves, so I have to plan my defenses carefully to not get easily chopped up into awakened meat.<br /> <br /> My question is, considering the &quot;spell stacking rules&quot; written on the spells section, can my thyrsus use life 3 &quot;honing the form&quot; to boost different attributes with multiple instances of the spell, without incurring in the spell stacking issue?<br /> <br /> For example, casting a honing spell to get +4 in strength and then another one to have +4 to dexterity? Since the rules are written specifically pointing to magic affecting the same aspect of a character (skill, attribute, etc..) I'm not sure if affecting differents attributes with the same spell counts as stacking<br /> <br /> <br /> Question n. 2 that I had reading through life Arcanum : can Animal minion work on other supernatural being?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","user":"Lasombra","date":". 06-23-2020, 04:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T03:57:37-07:00","id":1398321,"title":"","content":"Spell stacking (especially with Honing the Form) has been <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1385055\">discussed</a>.<br /> <br /> Question 2: Yeah, sure. There's generally no difference between supernatural beings and humans when it comes to spells except when there logically should be. (You can't, for example, use Animal Minion on vampires since they're dead.) Since Animal Minion works on humans, it would work just as well on werewolves. It won't, however, work with spirits (unless you add Spirit) since they (similar to vampires) don't have living bodies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T05:06:31-07:00","id":1398334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1398303-honing-the-form-multiple-times?p=1398321#post1398321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spell stacking (especially with Honing the Form) has been <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1385055&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">discussed</a>.<br /> <br /> Question 2: Yeah, sure. There's generally no difference between supernatural beings and humans when it comes to spells except when there logically should be. (You can't, for example, use Animal Minion on vampires since they're dead.) Since Animal Minion works on humans, it would work just as well on werewolves. It won't, however, work with spirits (unless you add Spirit) since they (similar to vampires) don't have living bodies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanx for the answer. So I guess the answer is.. It depends? There is a user that mentioned David stating that honing the form can be used to boost different attributes with different castings, but apart from that, everyone seems to have different opinions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T18:39:18-07:00","id":1398495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lasombra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1398303-honing-the-form-multiple-times?p=1398334#post1398334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanx for the answer. So I guess the answer is.. It depends? There is a user that mentioned David stating that honing the form can be used to boost different attributes with different castings, but apart from that, everyone seems to have different opinions.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends what you consider to be separate aspects of a character, personally i think strength, dex and stamina are 3 separate aspects of a character. So a honing the form spell for each wont stack, two honing the form's on strength however are trying to act on the same aspect of that character and therefore wouldn't stack. (There was something DaveB did say that reinforced this view somewhere but i cant remember where it ended with the mention that the reason you would want to cast homing with the reach to combine the stats was so you would use 1 spell control to boost multiple stats but if you had the spell control then 3 castings for each was fine)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 06-23-2020, 09:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T10:18:15-07:00","id":1398618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1398303-honing-the-form-multiple-times?p=1398321#post1398321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spell stacking (especially with Honing the Form) has been <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1385055&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">discussed</a>.<br /> <br /> Question 2: Yeah, sure. There's generally no difference between supernatural beings and humans when it comes to spells except when there logically should be. (You can't, for example, use Animal Minion on vampires since they're dead.) Since Animal Minion works on humans, it would work just as well on werewolves. It won't, however, work with spirits (unless you add Spirit) since they (similar to vampires) don't have living bodies.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing, If we assume that life 4 can affect other supernatural beings as well, does that mean that I can shapechange (as per &quot;shapechanging&quot; spell) another supernatural (living) being with life? So for example I can transform another mage or werewolf into a dog? That seems something like only life 5 could achieve","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T10:26:23-07:00","id":1398619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lasombra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1398303-honing-the-form-multiple-times?p=1398618#post1398618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing, If we assume that life 4 can affect other supernatural beings as well, does that mean that I can shapechange (as per &quot;shapechanging&quot; spell) another supernatural (living) being with life? So for example I can transform another mage or werewolf into a dog? That seems something like only life 5 could achieve</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as it doesn't interfere with any of their own abilities. You can absolutely transform another mage into a dog. There is no reason for involving Life 5 because you're not Making or Unmaking anything. Mage 2e has removed a lot of the arbitrary Arcanum requirements that doesn't fit with what the different Practices are supposed to do.<br /> The werewolf is already a shapeshifter so they would enter a Clash of Wills whenever they attempt to shift to another form. As an ST I might actually allow them to auto-win because of how integral shapeshifting is to werewolves, but that would be a house rule in favour of the werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}